\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar softer, but finds respite on U.S. data. \b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2003\par 00:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The dollar eased a bit against the yen in early Asia on Monday but held on to most of its gains after better than expected U.S. manufacturing data and confirmation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hindered by the possibility of war with Iraq, the dollar was trading at 119.84/89 yen  compared with 119.89 in late pre-weekend trade. On Friday, it rose to as high as 120.07. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was a touch softer against the euro, with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $1.0782/87  compared with $1.0761. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 129.21/33  yen against 129.03. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar was finding some respite after weeks of weakness over a possible conflict with Iraq and doubts over the health of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the dollar took heart from data showing the regional Chicago purchasing managers index rose more than expected to 56.0 in January, well above the consensus estimate of 52.6. A reading above 50 indicates an expansion in activity. \par \par \uc2  That number eclipsed a worse than expected final reading on U.S. consumer sentiment in January. \par \par \uc2  The University of Michigan's consumer sentiment survey fell to 82.4, below the forecast of 83.0 and under December's reading of 86.7. \par \par \uc2  Traders were awaiting more clues on the U.S. economy this week, with the Institute of Supply Management's January manufacturing index due on Monday and jobs data due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Economists expected the ISM manufacturing index to creep down to 53.0 after an upwardly revised December result of 55.2. \par \par \uc2  IRAQ, \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  "The dollar has found strong support, but there is little incentive to buy it aggressively as long as the Iraq factor remains," said a trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Top U.N. disarmament officials are expected to go to Baghdad at the end of the week despite a letter they wrote that appeared to put conditions on that trip, U.N. officials said. \par \par \uc2  The U.N. trip, expected on Saturday, falls a few days before another key report by inspectors to the U.N. Security Council on February 14. It may be their last report before the United States makes a final decision on whether to attack. \par \par \uc2  The yen was under pressure after Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it had covertly sold yen for dollars after mid-January to prevent its strength from dousing demand for exports and undercutting a fragile economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  A Ministry official said it bought $6 billion worth of dollars on several occasions, confirming rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had helped keep the dollar underpinned in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  It was the first yen-selling action under Japan's recently appointed top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...        Debt...      Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 