\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-INSTANT VIEW- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2003\par 11:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 31 (Reuters) - The following are immediate reactions of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders and analysts to Bank of Japan data released on Friday that indicated Japanese authorities sold yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  paid 678 billion yen to the private sector through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which mostly represents \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It would be the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since June 28 and the first under newly appointed Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi. \par \par \uc2  Most traders had not detected any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the month, although there was speculation that Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or at least checked rates, in New York and European trading hours on January 27. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  TOMOKO FUJII, ECONOMIST, NIKKO SALOMON SMITH BARNEY \par \par \uc2  "If there was in fact 'hidden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' here, I have to say I don't see its point. Finance Minister (Masajuro) Shiokawa has said that the government will warn the market when rates are volatile. But if they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tell no one, there would be little impact. Of course there are various ways to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the idea of 'hidden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' doesn't feel very right. I would question its effectiveness, as a policy. Of course one could question whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is effective at all at a time like this, when the root of the cause is not yen strength but dollar weakness." \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  KOJI FUKAYA, CHIEF \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ANALYST, BANK OF TOKYO-MITSUBISHI \par \par \uc2  "Judging by the figure, we can say that it is quite large. Given Japan's current account surplus of around one trillion yen every month, the volume is substantial, which shows \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong will to weaken the yen. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without immediate confirmation has been rare in recent years, and this may suggest that Japan is taking into consideration the new U.S. economic team, whose stance is not yet clear, by keeping a low profile this time." \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  MARSHALL GITTLER, SENIOR \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, DEUTSCHE BANK, TOKYO \par \par \uc2  "The market had assumed that that they did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so this should not have any effect to the market. It simply confirms market assumption." \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  STEVEN SAYWELL, \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST AT CITIBANK, LONDON \par \par \uc2  "We would've thought that if there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  you would publicise that to maximise the effect so it seems a little bit odd. The U.S. had never suggested they would weaken the dollar so there is little concern from the U.S. in Japan curbing the appreciation of the yen beyond 120. The yen did have a sharp rise but it was a difficult situation for the BOJ and MOF. They don't want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a situation where the dollar is weakening across the board because it's tricky." \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  DEREK HALPENNY, \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  ECONOMIST, BANK OF TOKYO MITSUBISHI, LONDON \par \par \uc2  "The data suggests that there may have been something but we cannot confirm that. Looking at the figures one could conclude that there has been some kind of activity to hold the markets up. What it means going forward is difficult to say. But we are of the view that there is more dollar weakness ahead, related to geopolitical issues. If you look at the overall flows regarding the yen, you have to remember the current account surplus. We have also seen some very tentative signs of Japanese selling of foreign assets in the weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data. If there is a covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking place it is not a very large quantity and if anything it will slow the move lower. In that context we still feel the risks are on the downside for the dollar." \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  HIDEAKI FURUMAYA, HEAD OF INTERBANK DESK, TRUST AND CUSTODY SERVICES BANK, TOKYO \par \par \uc2  "We still have to see whether the market is brave enough to buy the dollar above 119 yen with this news, but the market has turned clearly nervous about selling the dollar below 118 yen. At the time when the Japanese authorities were said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there were rumours that massive knock out options were placed at 117.25 yen. A break below that level may have spurred the dollar's downtrend. At the moment, it's difficult to tell whether the previous massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with an announcement, or the recent style without an immediate announcement is effective. We still have to wait and see. \par \par \uc2  "The past two regimes under (Eisuke) Sakakibara and (Haruhiko) Kuroda \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in large amounts, but there was always a question whether the new regime would take a similar approach. Announcing massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had major impact in the past, but at the same the effect ran out very quickly. It seems that the new approach is working. Also I think it's better in the current market sentiment not to disclose \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately because people want to sell the dollar on rallies. In this mood, I think it's better now not to tell whether the Japanese authorities have acted immediately because it can give more uncertainty, which seems to limit active dollar-selling." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030131dz1v00k2b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
