\par\par \b \uc2  Yen weakens against dollar after BOJ data. \b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2003\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 31 (Reuters) - The yen dipped against the dollar on Friday after data from the Bank of Japan showed Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 678 billion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had been waiting for the data, following widespread speculation on Friday that the BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been concerned that the buoyant yen would hinder Japan's export-led recovery, but traders said broad dollar losses and confusion over the U.S.' strong dollar policy made the Japanese authorities reluctant to admit any yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen weakened to 119.20/25 per dollar  by 1018 GMT, close to the day's lows and around 15 ticks below levels seen before the data release. It then reversed those losses. \par \par \uc2  The yen also slipped towards earlier 3-1/2 year lows against the euro of 129.09 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030131dz1v00jak\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
