\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar treads water, Camp David and BOJ data eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2003\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 31 (Reuters) - The dollar held above recent lows on Friday ahead of U.S.-British talks about war on Iraq and more U.S. data, with feverish interest in Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  data which could confirm talk \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen this month. \par \par \uc2  U.S. President George W. Bush and British Prime Minister Tony Blair will discuss strategy on forcing Baghdad to disarm at Camp David later on Friday, which would offer more information about the likelihood of a U.S.-led war against Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The greenback, after hitting a three-year low against the euro beyond $1.09  this week, held above that level even when key U.S. stock indices notched up steep losses on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts pointed out the dollar was in part helped by rumours that persistent dollar bids detected around 117.50 yen last week might have come from Japanese authorities, although there is no confirmation the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data on market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January will be released around 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "Covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if there was any, would be a response to uncertainty about the U.S. administration's stance on the dollar," said one trader at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. maintains it is sticking to its long-held strong dollar policy but many traders believe, given the dollar's steep slide recently, this stance may have been abandoned for now. \par \par \uc2  Japan on the other hand has made clear it does not want the yen to rise and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  publicly in May and June last year. \par \par \uc2  By 0845 GMT the dollar stood at $1.0823, little changed from late New York levels on Thursday. Against the yen it was at 119.10 , having reached its highest in almost three weeks near 120 in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  NEW STRATEGY? Some dealers say Japanese banks were seen buying $300 million each on two days, January 24 and 27, and the amount bought was thought to be at least $2 billion. \par \par \uc2  "The MOF didn't want to tell everybody because the dollar was coming off against everything. Politically, you can't be seen to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the dollar is down across the board," said a European bank trader in London. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it proved to be around the $2 billion mark, it was insufficient to turn the dollar/yen trend around. \par \par \uc2  "That amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only be to put a brake on and correct the speed of the dollar's decline against the yen, not enough to change the overall trend," said Koji Fukaya, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this marked the first yen selling action by the MOF under its recently-appointed top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi succeeded Haruhiko Kuroda on January 14. Under Kuroda, Japan stepped into the market on several occasions to stop the export-damaging yen rise but most of the time Japanese monetary officials confirmed their action. \par \par \uc2  A senior Finance Ministry official said on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not conduct drastic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guide the yen to a specific rate but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be done as a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  MORE DATA \par \par \uc2  The U.S. data calender is rather heavy and analysts expect the data would paint a more mixed picture about the world's biggest economy. \par \par \uc2  University of Michigan final January consumer sentiment survey, due at 1445 GMT is expected to read 83 against a final December reading of 86.7. \par \par \uc2  The Chicago Purchasing management index, due at 1500 GMT, is expected to rise to 52.6 in January from a revised 51.7 the month before, essentially playing catch-up to December's big gain in the national ISM survey. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030131dz1v00hae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
