\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's Hush-Hush  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Sparks USD Rally, For Now \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry \par \uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2003\par 18:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Sometimes softly, softly does it, as the yen's decline on Friday shows. \par \par \uc2  The announcement by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight that it undertook covert \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month to weaken the yen drove the Japanese  \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its biggest drop against the dollar in three weeks on Friday. It has left the greenback dancing around the important psychological Y120 mark, up from a session low  of Y118.88 and helped fire a broad-based dollar rebound. \par \par \uc2  As the world's second-biggest economy hovers on the brink of a renewed economic downturn, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the few recourses \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy makers have at their disposal to encourage growth. \par \par \uc2  But in the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the guardian of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy - has been much more open with its market forays. This time, the confirmation that it has been quietly stepping into the market marks a clear - and intelligent - shift that has already nervous \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders closely second-guessing any rapid slips in the yen. For a short while at least, this new deft strategy may continue to bear fruit, U.S.-based analysts say. \par \par \uc2  "This kind of stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is certainly not ordinary," said Marcel Kasumovich, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy with Merrill Lynch in New York. This shift  from the past track record of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's openly trumpeted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  marks a sea change, he said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese monetary authorities focused on slowing the speed of the yen's appreciation against the dollar and in the very near term at least "they have been successful", Kasumovich said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government sold about Y700 billion, (close to $6 billion) in several rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during January and stands ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively to rein in excessive movements in the yen, a senior ministry official told reporters in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "Recent (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) moves had been volatile and we saw a need to take action," the official said. "Hypothetically speaking, if excessive moves had continued,  we could have conducted a large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  This latest change of tack by the Japanese government - which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly to the tune of a hefty $30 billion during May and June - is causing some major \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2   market participants to bet more heavily that the yen will decline. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Music For Yen Bears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Robert Sinche, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Citibank - the biggest\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bank - said Friday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's  new approach to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "is positive news for yen bears." He said it was a\par significant factor in Citibank's decision to take positions in the\par market Friday, based on the expectation that the euro will appreciate\par further against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier Friday, the euro jumped to global session peaks   around\par Y129.40, breaking its highest levels since May 1999. The dollar hit an\par intraday high of Y120.04, almost a full yen higher than Y119.03 late\par Thursday in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the dollar generally holding up fairly well against  the yen last\par week - despite a broader fall against other key rivals - many \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders had speculated that the Bank of Japan may have been\par seeking to influence the exchange rate. But many had assumed that, in\par the absence  of any immediate confirmation by Japan, other factors may\par have been driving choppy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance ministry traditionally confirms \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shortly\par after carrying it out, via the BOJ.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Of course, despite the short-term headway \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have  gained with\par its new under-the-radar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactic, over time it "becomes a\par more blunt instrument," said Kasumovich.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , by their nature, need to keep surprising market\par participants in order to keep having a pronounced effect on exchange\par rates, particularly in a market of this size. The ramifications of\par Japan's continued willingness to act in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets may also spread\par beyond the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Newly confirmed U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow has already\par indicated he opposes such actions by governments in the financial\par markets. Analysts think this might result in some tensions with Japan's\par policy makers at an upcoming meeting of finance ministers from the Group\par of Seven major industrialized economies in late February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I favor reliance on open exchange markets and think that the trading\par system of the world is best placed by having \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that reflect\par their inherent value," Snow said this week, written answers to questions\par from the Senate  Finance Committee.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We may get some more flares at the G7 meeting than usual," said\par Kasumovich.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By John Parry; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Miyako Takebe and James Simms in Tokyo contributed to this report).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030131dz1v007pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
