\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar soft after bouncing on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  rumours. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2003\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 28 (Reuters) - The dollar was under pressure against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia on Tuesday after shooting up overnight on talk that the Federal Reserve, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had either checked rates or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported a rumour of large-scale bids from just one Japanese source overnight when the dollar was falling towards 117.50 yen, with the orders rumoured to be from the Bank of Japan (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  "Various rumours were rife last night such as the Fed and the ECB selling euros against dollars, and the Fed checking dollar/yen rates," said Yoshihiko Kobayashi, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales principal at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "I'm sceptical about the talk, but whether true or not, it was enough to cause a short-covering wave in the market, which has been massively short of dollars," he said. \par \par \uc2  Having bounced to a high of 119.30 yen in New York on Monday from a low of 117.55 yen, the dollar settled back to 118.36/41 yen as of 0259 GMT. It had ended New York trade at around 118.45/53 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0838/42 and 128.29/40 yen after edging up to three-year highs of $1.0907 and 128.97 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market grew nervous about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Bundesbank President and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  member Ernst Welteke said on Monday it would be a worrying sign if the dollar fell too quickly against the euro. \par \par \uc2  He echoed European Union Monetary Affairs Commissioner Pedro Solbes, who said on Friday that the speed of the euro's rise was a cause for concern. \par \par \uc2  WAITING FOR SNOW AND BUSH \par \par \uc2  Following a U.N. report on Iraqi arms inspections on Monday, the market is now expecting that a U.S.-led attack on Iraq could take place as early as end-February. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, market participants expect the dollar to fall further. \par \par \uc2  "The U.N. inspectors' dismal stories and the negative reaction from the U.S. suggest that that war in Iraq is increasingly likely," said Marshall Gittler, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deustche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "However, the U.S. has to play for time to get its troops into place and the most likely time for invasion is end-February to early March. That's plenty more time for the dollar to weaken further," he said. \par \par \uc2  In the near term, participants are waiting for U.S. Treasury Secretary designate John Snow's confirmation hearing in Congress later in the day to confirm U.S. dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  The market is also waiting for President George W. Bush's State of the Union speech at 0200 GMT on Wednesday (9 p.m. Tuesday local time). \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar could come under pressure if Bush hints at a unilateral attack, or at least an attack involving a restricted number of allies. \par \par \uc2  If the U.S. has to bear the brunt of a hefty war bill, it would pile further pressure on the rapidly deteriorating U.S. budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami's comments that the yen could not be weakened by Japan alone and that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should be determined by the market, reflecting economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Likewise, it was little moved by Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa's remarks that he wanted to guide the yen down towards purchasing power parity - a much lower level than at present. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030128dz1s00dm3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
