\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Spikes Sharply Across Brd Ahead of Blix Presentation \b0\par\par\uc2  By Grainne McCarthy \par \uc2 916 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2003\par 15:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar leaped swiftly across the board early Monday while Treasury prices slid, amid a slew of speculation about a potential war with Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The speed of the dollar's appreciation caught many market participants by surprise, leaving them scrambling for  an explanation. Several dealers said the clearest possible catalyst for the gains was a renewed rumor that Iraqi leader  Saddam Hussein would choose exile over war, while others pointed to the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, so far there has been no concrete evidence of any action by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rumor of Saddam's exile was also the key factor behind the selloff in  Treasurys, which has erased all of the market's earlier gains. \par \par \uc2  "Rumors - none of them particularly credible - are moving the market this morning and I don't think they will have any lasting impact on bond prices," said Andrew Brenner, head of institutional fixed income at Investec Ernst in New York. \par \par \uc2  "We're going to see a lot of this during the week" because there is so much speculation about Iraq, and the Federal Reserve's meeting results, said Brenner. \par \par \uc2  Others said the sharp market moves reflected a rush to prepare for a scenario under which chief U.N. weapons inspector Hans Blix will argue for more time to carry out inspections in Iraq, an argument that could go some way towards winning more time for the U.S. to gain broader international backing for a war. \par \par \uc2  Blix will present an intensely anticipated report to the  U.N. Security Council regarding his team's work searching for weapons of mass destruction in Iraq at around 10:30 a.m.  EST (1530 GMT). \par \par \uc2  "A few punters are taking money off the table before Blix talks," said Thomas Molloy, a trader at Bank Leumi in New York. \par \par \uc2  Shortly before 9:00 a.m. EST, the dollar began soaring against the yen, swiftly replicating that move against other  major rivals. The dollar was at Y118.35 against the yen, quite steeply up from Y117.83 earlier in the morning, while the euro had slipped to $1.0812, steeply down from $1.0864 shortly before 9:00 a.m. EST. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at $1.3571, up from $1.3499, while the pound was at $1.6319 down from $1.6350. \par \par \uc2  At 9:35 a.m. EST, the benchmark 10-year note was down 3/32 at 100 15/32 to yield 3.94%, significantly lower than the level an hour ago when the issue was up 7/32 at 100 25/32 to yield 3.90%. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the 30-year bond was down 15/32 at 107 12/32 to yield 4.89%, compared with 4.82% earlier in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The five-year note was unchanged at 100 17/32 to yield 2.88%, compared with 2.82% earlier, while the two-year note was also unchanged at 100 6/32 to yield 1.64%, compared with \par \par \uc2  Paul Calvetti, head of government bond trading at Deutsche Bank in New York, said he has seen mostly sellers in the past hour in the Treasury market even though volume hasn't been particularly heavy. \par \par \uc2  "It could be that people are anticipating that once we get the Hans Blix report there might be squaring of positions," he said. \par \par \uc2  The swift moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market also came  amid talk that the Federal Reserve had been ringing around to some trading desks to check exchange rates, a tactic that  in the past has had the very specific function of seeking to introduce some two-sided risk into exchange rates, without actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Other traders said the Fed hadn't been checking rates, but had simply been seeking to find out why the dollar was jumping so swiftly. An official at the New York Federal Reserve declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Clearly, the pace of the dollar's jump - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spiked by over one yen in just an hour - has sparked speculation that the BOJ might be in the market; some traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past week. \par \par \uc2  With a languishing economy at home, Japanese policy makers have made no secret of their desire for a weaker yen,  although many market participants believe they have held off on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they would have had to fight a tide of  broad-based dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  Still, banks that would usually be able to see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  via their trading systems haven't reported any so far. "I haven't heard anything I would believe in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Molloy, at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  More broadly, the volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets reflects the stream of potentially highly significant events this week that could move U.S. asset prices. \par \par \uc2  After Blix's presentation Monday, Tuesday will be dominated by Senate confirmation hearings for Treasury Secretary nominee John Snow and President George W. Bush's State of The Union address later in the day. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the Security Council is due to discuss Blix's report, while the Federal Open Market Committee will also make a decision on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  -Grainne McCarthy; Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2381; grainne.mccarthy@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (John Parry, Steven Vames and Joy Shaw contributed to this report) \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 28038 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030127dz1r002s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
