\par\par \b \uc2  IMM speculators grow huge net long position - CFTC. \b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2003\par 23:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Kyle Peterson\par     CHICAGO, Jan 24 (Reuters) - Speculators of IMM yen futures\par extended an already monstrous net long position from Jan. 15 to\par Jan. 21, according to data released on Friday.\par     The condition underscored the potential for a yen decline\par from five-month highs reached last week. But analysts cautioned\par that an inflated speculative position is only a small piece of a\par much larger puzzle and that the fundamental factors that have\par been weighing on the dollar/yen in recent months are still in\par place.\par     The Commodity Futures Trading Commission's Commitments of\par Traders data on speculative positioning is used by many analysts\par as a reverse indicator of future market direction. For example,\par extreme net long speculative positions often presage a decline\par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially if that position conflicts with\par those held by the more influential commercial players.\par  \par     Speculators generally comprise trend followers seeking to\par pick a precise top or bottom in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The CFTC data revealed a net long yen position of 33,293\par contracts, up from 32,944 contracts in the previous week.\par     "You have to put everything into context, and that is that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar is under pressure from every angle," said David\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mozina, director of global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Bank of America.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But the spec market is very, very bearish the dollar. That does\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par make me a little concerned about recent moves and how much more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it can continue."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The last time the net long yen position was so large was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November 1999. At that time the dollar was trading near 102 yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  . About a month later, the dollar mounted a two-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uptrend that took the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  nearly to 111 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar has been on the ropes against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falling to a three-year low vs. the euro on Friday, and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par five-month low of 117.37 yen on Jan. 17. The dollar has hovered\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par just above that level vs. the yen this week, while falling to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some yen traders believe the Japanese government may step in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to sell the yen lower if its growing strength takes a toll on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that country's export market. An extremely large net long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position by yen speculators could give Japan the ammunition it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par needs to knock down that net position through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Friday, Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Masaru Hayami said the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would watch the impact of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Japanese economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Now the positions appear to be getting extended on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculative side, people betting on the stronger yen," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mozina of the large speculative position. "Maybe if the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials are thinking about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , you've got a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par classic bear trap for these players to get squashed."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par March yen were mostly steady during the CFTC's reporting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par period, slipping from a close of $0.008487 on Jan. 15 to a close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of $0.008480 on Jan. 21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculators in euro futures, meanwhile, trimmed a net long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position to 28,442 contracts from 28,773 contracts in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previous week. The net long position remained within striking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par distance of the Nov. 12 reading, which was the largest net long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position since reaching a record 35,433 contracts in May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     March euros have been soaring since December and rose from a\par close of $1.0520 on Jan. 15 to a close of $1.0692 on Jan. 21.\par     "It's at lofty levels," Mozina said of the net long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position. "It's close to levels that are the greatest since the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inception of the euro. So I still think there is still more room\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the upside."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030124dz1o016li\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
