\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slides to new lows as U.S. stocks tumble. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 977 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2003\par 19:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 24 (Reuters) - The dollar fell hard on Friday as a rout in U.S. stock prices exacerbated the negative sentiment toward a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  already tainted by the growing possibility of war with Iraq. \par \par \uc2  "The stock market is the big story," said John Beerling, chief dealer at Wells Fargo in Minneapolis. "Stocks had a nice start to the year, but now have been down for most of the last several days and the dollar is more or less following that. \par \par \uc2  "But talk of war continues to be behind it all," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Dow dropped almost three percent and the tech-heavy Nasdaq was off more than three percent as investors took flight, frightened by the prospect of a U.S. attack on Iraq and further dismayed by bleak earnings from utility firms. \par \par \uc2  The Dow is now back to levels of last October. \par \par \uc2  Most economists believe that a short military conflict in Iraq would do little harm to the U.S. economy, although a drawn-out campaign could be hurtful. \par \par \uc2  But even a short war could depress capital flows into U.S. assets if foreign investors opt for the safe bet and keep cash at home. \par \par \uc2  By early afternoon, the euro was up 0.80 percent against the dollar at $1.0846 , new session and three-year highs. \par \par \uc2  For a while, euro gains were contrained by options positions at the $1.08 mark. \par \par \uc2  "We certainly ran into resistance right around the $1.08 level, but once we went through it was pretty much off to the races," said Beerling. \par \par \uc2  It was the seventh time in seven days the euro posted new three-year highs against the dollar. The dollar also lost more ground to the Swiss franc. It was off 0.80 percent to 1.3513 francs , new four-year lows. \par \par \uc2  IRAQ ATTACK? \par \par \uc2  The White House has been building its case against Iraq and trying to build support among fellow members of the U.N. Security Council, many of which have expressed strong opposition to taking action against Iraq at this time. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. State Department on Friday said it had "very convincing evidence" Iraq possessed banned weapons and Undersecretary of State John Bolton said the information would be made public "at an appropriate time." \par \par \uc2  The United States' renewed pressure on Iraq sent oil prices higher and helped gold spurt to a new six-year high. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was reluctant to hold dollars ahead of next week's key events, which include a report to the Security Council on Monday by U.N. weapons inspectors and U.S. President George W. Bush's State of the Union speech on Tuesday evening. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody wants to be long dollars going into the weekend, with the major political events that are coming next week," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  Other important events on next week's calendar include Senate confirmation hearings for Treasury Secretary-designate John Snow and a meeting of the Federal Reserve's policy board. \par \par \uc2  NOT JUST GEOPOLITICS \par \par \uc2  While the threat of war was the overriding factor driving the dollar, dealers said there were also signs investors with a longer-term view were favoring euros over the dollar. \par \par \uc2  They said signs of improvement in the euro zone economy and European leaders' seeming comfort with the euro's level was encouraging euro purchases, even against the safe-haven Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  "Even the worst overbought conditions can go on for some time as long as there is real money flowing," noted Malpede. \par \par \uc2  Sterling also was benefiting from good economic data, even though Britain, the chief ally of the United States, would be expected to see its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffer along with the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Much stronger than expected UK retail sales data released on Thursday, a healthy British growth report for fourth quarter 2002 and speculation Russia, which said on Thursday it wanted to cut back on dollar reserves, might favor sterling for its higher yield, were factors boosting the pound, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the U.K. can print decent numbers, it's hard to hammer sterling," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2  The pound was trading at $1.6335 , up 0.64 percent. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as low as 117.56 yen , shy of four-month lows of 117.37 yen touched last week. In early afternoon, it was trading at 117.70 yen, off 0.30 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would carefully watch the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves on the Japanese economy, but noted also that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements could not be manipulated easily. \par \par \uc2  The market has been on guard for possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from appreciating too fast and hurting its export sector. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 1816GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par calculated from the levels at 5:30 p.m. (22:30 GMT) in the\par previous New York session.\par                       Last  US Close    %      YTD     2002\par                              23 Jan.  Change %Change    Close\par -----