\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Short Covering Pushes Dlr, Euro Up Against Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2003\par 06:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Short covering pushed the dollar higher against the yen in Asia Thursday, in what market participants say is becoming a familiar pattern. \par \par \uc2  The session was almost a mirror image of Tuesday's Asian trading, when a flurry of buying by Japanese trust banks and U.S. funds triggered stop-loss orders in the morning and sent the pair to almost exactly the same high - Y118.83 Thursday - before Japanese exporter selling emerged and cut the rally short. \par \par \uc2  And in another deja vu from Tuesday, buying from the same quarters led the euro to spike against the yen. Thursday's Asian session high was Y127.23 - within a whisper of the euro's all-time record high of Y127.36 set in June 1999. \par \par \uc2  "Just like earlier this week, there weren't any big trading factors. It was all positioning again today," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar remains vulnerable to such rapid short covering moves, traders said, as many strategists still recommend shorting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on signs that U.S.-led military action in Iraq could be imminent, as well as on concerns about the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  "Rising war rhetoric clearly kept investors on a bearish bias toward U.S. assets," said a J.P. Morgan daily research report. "Against this backdrop, we want to stay short dollars tactically." \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y118.73 , above Y118.31 in New York and Y118.19 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0717, lower than $1.0725 in New York and $1.0733 in Tokyo Wednesday. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y127.24, compared with Wednesday's Y126.89 in New York and Y126.85 in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6165, down from $1.6177 in New York but slightly higher than $1.6163 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar began to fall from its session highs after Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa suggested in parliamentary questioning that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer on red alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  "It's not good for the government to respond actively to moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to achieve the rate it wants," Shiokawa told lawmakers, despite the fact that an overly strong yen is bad for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-oriented manufacturers. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were aimed at sudden market fluctuations rather than attempts to achieve a given exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Given the dollar's rise of more than one yen from its low of Y117.40 hit last Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears have somewhat dissipated, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro lost ground, succumbing to cross-trading pressure as the dollar gained against the yen. But support at $1.0700 held in Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  "Fundamentally, the euro is still a good buy against the dollar, so this trend isn't likely to last long," said a European bank trader in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan underscored Japan's precarious fundamentals in its economic assessment for January, repeating in its monthly report that the economy has bottomed but is showing no sign of recovery. \par \par \uc2  "The economy is unlikely to show clear signs of recovery for some time, since exports and production are expected to be virtually unchanged for the time being, while restraining forces such as excess labor input and debt persist," the BOJ said in the report. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also remains concerned about possible downside risks from a weak global economy and a negative impact from any further falls in Japanese stock prices and from banks' bad loan disposals. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030123dz1n000am\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
