\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Surges Half A Yen On Short-Covering \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2003\par 06:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar surged half a yen in Asia Monday as overseas speculators unwound their long yen positions and some Japanese players bought the greenback to meet corporate demand. \par \par \uc2  Fears that the Japanese authorities may capitalize on the huge overhang of long yen positions in the International Money Market of the Chicago Mercantile Exchange to maximize the impact of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spurred short-covering, lifting the dollar as high as Y118.32, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The constant barrage of warnings from Japanese finance ministry officials against yen strength during the dollar's recent fall to a four-month low have put the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on high alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the past, the finance ministry has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the markets were extremely short dollars, thereby increasing the effectiveness of their \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting the massively long yen positions against the dollar, the latest IMM commitment of traders report showed net yen long non-commercial positions were 32,944 contracts in the week to Jan. 14, up from 27,227 contracts in the previous week. \par \par \uc2  Some Japanese banks, on behalf of Japanese corporations, also joined in the dollar buying toward the 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing, helping to boost the dollar above the psychological Y118 level in early trading. \par \par \uc2  As London-based overseas players are likely to follow through on more dollar short-covering after the opening of European trade, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could rise as far as its Jan. 15 high of Y118.70 later in the session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y118.29, above Y117.78 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y118.13 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0643, lower than $1.0666 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.0615 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y125.86, up from Y125.62 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y125.37 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Y116 and Y117 if this area is reached by the end of January, given that the technical charts show key support at the Y115.50-Y115.80 level, Goldman Sachs said in a recent research report, noting any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that fails to support the dollar above this level would be "concerning." \par \par \uc2  But, the authorities may be in a difficult position to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless market sentiment, gauged by Goldman Sachs' risk-reversals index and the IMM positions, clearly shift to short dollar positions, according to the report. \par \par \uc2  As a result, if the dollar threatens the Y116-Y117 area and these two indicators tilt toward short dollar positions in the near term, the authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Goldman said. \par \par \uc2  While the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be supported by ongoing fears of MOF yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the greenback is also likely to be weighed on by lingering geopolitical concerns and uncertainty over the U.S. economic recovery, said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar should trade sideways in a Y117.50-Y121.00 range this week," he said. \par \par \uc2  This week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets will watch the Bank of Japan's two-day policy board meeting starting Tuesday and keep an eye out for any fresh developments on the geopolitical front, Umemoto added. \par \par \uc2  Although market consensus is that BOJ will stand pat on monetary policy, Umemoto said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could decide to downgrade its economic assessment for January, which is due out Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A downgrade in the BOJ's economic assessment would be a yen-negative factor as it would provide more evidence that the nation's economic recovery has stalled after the government lowered its assessment of the economy for the third consecutive month late last week. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6098, down from $1.6138 in New York and lower than $1.6099 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030120dz1k0009d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
