\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slides alongside slipping U.S. stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kyle Peterson \par \uc2 860 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2003\par 19:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Updates prices, adds comments, changes dateline, previous NEW YORK) \par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Jan 15 (Reuters) - The dollar softened on Wednesday as U.S. stocks sagged, but dealers said technical resistance and expectations for Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were keeping dollar losses in check. \par \par \uc2  The greenback edged lower against the euro and fell against the yen, taking a lead from equities brought lower by Intel Corp.'s (INTC.O) announcement that it will slash capital spending this year, despite reporting better-than-expected fourth-quarter earnings late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar was up overnight but has given up those gains due to weakness on Wall Street," said Alex Beuzelin, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst at Ruesch International. \par \par \uc2  "Overall we're dealing with a day of general consolidation. I think we'll probably hold to this range today," he said. "Traders were looking to book some profits on the dollar's recent fall." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By midday in New York, the dollar was down slightly vs. both the euro and\par the Swiss franc, trading at $1.0582 euros per dollar  and 1.3814 francs\par . The dollar also was down to 117.89 yen       .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro traders noted technical resistance at $1.0600. That level also was said\par to be protected by some options-related selling.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options dealers have reported a double no-touch option with boundaries at\par $1.0175 and $1.1000. A double no-touch option is profitable if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par stays between two assigned prices. The option holder takes a payout if the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stays within the range until the option expires in four months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. economic data released on Wednesday were mixed. Manufacturing growth in\par New York state accelerated for a third straight month in January, offering\par hope that hard-hit factories elsewhere in the country may show some signs of\par strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But data on producer prices for December underscored the pricing problems\par faced by the nation's manufacturers. Wholesale prices were flat in December\par overall. But they fell 0.3 percent excluding the volatile food and energy\par sectors, largely because of falling vehicle prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Later Wednesday, the Federal Reserve is scheduled to offer more insights\par into the U.S. economy with its Beige Book report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Markets are pretty thin, and I think we are seeing some hedge fund\par players," said Lara Rhame, U.S. economist at Brown Brothers Harriman in New\par York. "And stocks being down certainly doesn't help the dollar."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers were looking ahead to the January Philadelphia Federal Reserve\par survey on U.S. mid-Atlantic manufacturing due for release on Thursday. The\par report was expected to show continued expansion in the sector.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Wall Street, the Intel news hurt the Nasdaq Composite Index , which was\par down 1.7 percent around 1 p.m. EST (1800 GMT). The Dow Jones industrial\par average  was down 1.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THREAT OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LOOMS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar shot higher in Asian trade, moving as high as 118.82 yen during\par Tokyo hours, prompting concern that the Bank of Japan might be in the\par markets selling yen. Officials in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have indicated a willingness to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the rise of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Some leaders have said a\par strong yen is a detriment to the Japanese export market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar quickly returned those gains, and it became clear that the spike\par was due to a big order or two during the quiet lunchtime period. A Finance\par Ministry official declined to comment on the move, which the market\par interpreted as meaning authorities had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "When the BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and it will at some point, it will be quite clear\par that they are signaling the market," noted Marc Chandler, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at HSBC.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Wednesday, Japan's newly appointed vice finance minister for\par international affairs, Zembei Mizoguchi, said he intended to stick to the\par policy on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates followed by his, predecessor, Haruhiko Kuroda.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mizoguchi restated the ministry line that it would take appropriate action\par on excessive movements in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 12:53 p.m. EST (1753 GMT). All data taken\par from Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT)\par in the previous New York session.\par Last     US Close   %     YTD %   2002\par 14 Jan.  Change  Change  Close\par ---------------------------------------------------------