\par\par \b \uc2  South Korea's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  holds interest rates \b0\par\par\uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2003\par 07:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Following are some of the main Asian business news stories\par (all times GMT)\par - - - -\par ECONOMIES\par SEOUL - South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds interest rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steady near a record low as mounting tensions in Iraq and North\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Korea's nuclear ambitions leave policy makers with little room \par \par \uc2  to act against surging property prices. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (ECONOMY-KOREA-RATES (WRAPUP 1), BY KIM KYOUNG-WHA, EXPECT\par BY 0800)\par TOKYO - Japan's government may announce within days who\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will be the next governor of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a crucial part\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of its strategy to revive a struggling economy and tackle\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (ECONOMY-JAPAN-BOJ, BY JONATHAN STANDING, EXPECT BY 0700)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG - Hong Kong residents blast the government for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its plan to hike taxes, saying it's doing nothing to help them\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as they struggle to cope with an economic downturn.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (HONGKONG (UPDATE 2), BY TAN EE LYN, EXPECT BY 0700,\par PICTURE)\par GUANGZHOU, China - Move over Shanghai and Beijing. China's\par third city, Guangzhou, is spending $9 billion on a spate of\par glitzy projects designed to dazzle the eye.\par (ECONOMY-CHINA-GUANGZHOU, BY DOUG YOUNG, MOVED)\par SINGAPORE - Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warns of tough times\par ahead for the island state's manufacturers and says\par unemployment is set to climb from its current 15-year high.\par (ECONOMY-SINGAPORE (UPDATE 1), BY JACQUELINE WONG, MOVED)\par - - - -\par MARKETS\par SINGAPORE - Asian stocks droop as chip makers slump on a\par dour outlook and a weaker dollar hurts exporters, compounding\par gloom over a fall in U.S. shares.\par (MARKETS-ASIA (WRAPUP 2), BY RICHARD BAUM, EXPECT BY 0700)\par TOKYO - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , worried by a strengthening yen, keeps up its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market but the effect seems\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to wearing thin as authorities have yet to follow threatening\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par words with action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (ECONOMY-JAPAN-KURODA (UPDATE 1), MOVED)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO - A Japanese 10-year government bond auction draws\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong bids even though its 0.9 percent interest rate matches\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the lowest ever for such paper; the auction produces a record\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volume of bids for the amount of paper on offer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MARKETS-JAPAN-AUCTION (UPDATE 1), MOVED)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MANILA - The Philippines, short of cash and investor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confidence, clings to a rare spot of good news from Moody's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors Service after its $500 million global bond offering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falls a third short of target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (PHILIPPINES (WRAPUP 1), BY JOHN O'CALLAGHAN, EXPECT BY\par 0800)\par BANGKOK - Thai Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak says\par the government is looking for alternatives to a planned $1\par billion global bond issue which might be scrapped.\par (MARKETS-THAILAND-BONDS (UPDATE 1), MOVED)\par - - - -\par COMPANIES\par TOKYO - Japan's investment bankers are betting that a wave\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of corporate restructuring will halt the slide in merger\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par business as companies revamp \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plagued by weak sales,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par heavy debts and excess capacity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (FINANCIAL-JAPAN-MERGERS, BY MIKI SHIMOGORI, MOVED)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO - Japan's Yamaha Motor, the world's second-largest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par motorcycle maker, expects its global shipments to rise 20\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in 2003 as booming sales in Asia counter a sluggish\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic market and slower growth in the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (AUTOS-JAPAN-YAMAHA (UPDATE 2), BY DANIEL HAUCK, EXPECT BY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0700) SINGAPORE - Costly battle between two reclusive Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par magnates for control of cash-rich Singapore takeover target\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NatSteel looks set to last beyond Friday when an offer by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chinese-Malaysian hotelier Ong Beng Seng expires.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MINERALS-SINGAPORE-NATSTEEL, BY DOREEN SIOW, EXPECT BY\par 0800)\par SEOUL - A faster-than-expected fall in chip prices and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible increase in supply send the shares of Samsung\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Electronics, the world's largest memory chip maker, falling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par five percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (TECH-KOREA-SAMSUNG (UPDATE 1), BY KIM YEON-HEE, EXPECT BY\par 0700)\par - - - -\par If you have any queries, please call:\par Singapore (65) 6870-3813\par Comments to: asia.newseds@reuters.com.