\par\par \b \uc2  Yen lower after  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  warns of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2002\par 04:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0300 GMT - Dollar rebounds marginally against the yen after Japanese officials say they may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  even during the New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  - Yen off the morning's 3-= month high of 118.34 after the comments \par \par \uc2  - A Japanese finance ministry source said Japan will take necessary action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to counter volatility, even with the markets closed for week-long New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  - Traders had taken the yen up from 120 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar however still stuck at a three-year low of $1.0480/85 against the euro , weakened by the prospect of war with Iraq and a brewing confrontation with North Korea. U.S. data showing slower manufacturing growth and a drop in housing sales also hurts the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Singapore dollar  shrugs off the yen's gains overnight and moves in Asian trading, concentrating instead on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's policy announcement due on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  - Traders in Singapore report U.S. dollar bids in the local market as players brace for a possible monetary easing through a widening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted band. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021231dycv005k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
