\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar's Drop Vs Yen Heightens  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Alert \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tyler Lifton \par \uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2002\par 19:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- A sharp drop in the dollar's value  against the yen early Monday in New York has put the market  on heightened alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though analysts say there are reasons to believe the Japanese government won't take direct action before the new year. \par \par \uc2  Blowing through a couple of levels that had been providing technical and option-related support, the dollar sank as low as Y118.31 Monday in New York from a global high  around Y120.00 in Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  Analysts cited different reasons for the dollar's renewed weakness against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after several days during which it had remained soft but fairly stable. \par \par \uc2  Unwinding of bearish yen positions against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the euro and the U.K. pound, propped the  yen up and led to its rise against the dollar early Monday,  said Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC Securities in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro had a solid run against the yen in recent days,  before taking a dip Monday. The euro was trading at 123.61 last Monday, then rose as high as Y125.49 Friday before skidding to Y123.82 Monday morning in New York and trading at Y124.10 early Monday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Many Japanese traders "are trying to square up (investment positions) or maybe take some profits going into  the prolonged holiday," Lara Rhame, senior economist at Brown Brothers Harriman in New York said of the activity that led to the yen's strength Monday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese financial markets will remain closed until next  Monday in observance of the traditional New Year holidays. With virtually all the world's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closed on January 1, volume dries to only a fraction of normal activity during the last days of the year. Thin market conditions cause exaggerated movements and make it difficult for traders to determine short-term trends. \par \par \uc2  Last week, even as it was swooning to multi-year lows against the euro, Swiss franc and the pound, the dollar remained relatively firm against the yen, in part because of  fears that any attempt to push the dollar decisively below the Y120 mark would prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On several occasions last week, Japanese officials verbally threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the yen continue appreciating against the greenback. The dollar remained in a range of Y119.81 to Y120.76 during the Christmas week. \par \par \uc2  But officials in Japan remained silent early Monday, even as the dollar fell to its weakest level against the yen  since September 9. Japan prefers a weaker yen to help its exporting community, the peg on which hopes of economic growth in the world's second largest economy rests. \par \par \uc2  The Y118 area to which the dollar fell to Monday "is not a very workable level for Japanese exporters," said T.J. Marta, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst for Citibank in New York. \par \par \uc2  That fact, combined with the rapid drop in the dollar against the yen Monday, increases the potential for Japanese  \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Against the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was mildly weaker Monday, weighed down by a disappointing report  on business activity in the Chicago region as well as weaker-than-expected U.S. home sales in November. \par \par \uc2  But several analysts believe that the signs are not pointing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the new year. Regardless of the yen's rise against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, its strength  against the dollar is in large part a function of broad dollar weakness in the face of geopolitical tension, making it something beyond Japan's ability to correct. \par \par \uc2  "If what seems to be a general weak dollar environment transforms into a (generalized) yen move" higher, then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become a very real threat, said HSBC's Chandler. "But I don't think we're there yet." \par \par \uc2  The closure of Japanese markets until Monday next week also mitigates a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Moreover, the fact that Japanese officials opted not to try to talk the yen weaker Monday - a step they frequently take before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  - may signal a decision to stay their hand for now. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect them to try and talk tough before they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Brown Brothers Harriman's Rhame. \par \par \uc2  Early afternoon in New York, the dollar is trading at Y118.47, somewhat above its intraday low but down sharply from Y119.90 late Friday. The euro is trading at $1.0470, up  from $1.0434 late Friday. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar is valued at CHF1.3882 down from CHF1.3906 late Friday, while the pound was trading at $1.6048, up slightly from $1.6033. \par \par \uc2  -By Tyler Lifto