\par\par \b \uc2  IMM speculators move to net long vs yen - CFTC. \b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2002\par 00:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NEW YORK, Dec 27 (Reuters) - Speculators in major IMM\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  futures reversed a net short position in the yen to a\par net long position while trimming net longs in the euro and\par raising them in the Swiss franc, data released on Friday\par showed.\par     The Commodity Futures Trading Commission's Commitments of\par Traders report on speculative positioning is used by many\par analysts as a reverse indicator of future market direction.\par Extreme net long speculative positions, for example, often\par presage a decline in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially if that position\par conflicts with those held by the more influential players.\par  \par     Speculators generally comprise trend followers seeking to\par pick a precise top or bottom in the market.\par     The release normally would compile data from Wednesday\par through the following Tuesday, but the latest data runs only\par until Monday, because of the Christmas holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Speculators in March yen futures reversed a net short\par position of 706 contracts to a net long position of 3,807\par contracts.\par     "Speculators were buying yen aggressively in the latest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, which is interesting because Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surely is not going to overlook signs of a market that is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressively long yen," said Delano.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been threatening to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell yen for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars to depress the export-hurting strength of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be more effective if the market were long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen and short dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par March yen shot higher during the reporting period from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close of $0.008288 on Dec. 18 to a close of $0.008331 on Dec.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 23.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Speculators in March euros cut net long positions to 28,127\par contracts from 30,601 contracts.\par     March euros were unchanged during the CFTC's reporting\par period, closing at $1.0222 on both Dec. 18 and Dec. 23.\par     Speculators in sterling futures cut net long positions to\par 6,901 contracts from 7,757 contracts in the previous week.\par     March sterling futures fell during the reporting period\par from a close of $1.5908 on Dec. 18 to a close of $1.5828 on\par Dec. 23.\par     Speculators in March Swiss francs increased net long\par positions to 21,823 contracts from 19,195.\par     March Swiss franc futures rose during the reporting period\par from a close of $0.7026 on Dec. 18 to a close of $0.7055 on\par Dec. 23.\par     "Speculators have been showing a good deal of appetite to\par buy Swiss...and the price action toward the end of this week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shows they are able to sustain that," said Andrew Delano,\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at IDEAGlobal. Swiss franc futures\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closed at $0.7148 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But once the non-speculative buying dries up, the pullback\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could be rather sharp," said Delano, adding "all of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are carrying relatively swollen long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions on them.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the Canadian dollar, speculators trimmed net long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions in the reporting week to 23,062 contracts from 23,613\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contracts. But Delano said the market still remained very long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Canadian dollars, perhaps setting itself up for a fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's very unlikely that the Canadian dollar can find a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par very good footing in coming weeks...there are troublesome signs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the Canadian dollar, especially with war tom-toms playing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and with risk aversion creeping up," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canadian dollar March futures were unchanged during the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reporting period at $0.6419 but have since fallen sharply,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closing at $0.6398 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021227dycr016wh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
