\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls to lows vs euro on N. Korea worries. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 955 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2002\par 00:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 27 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to its lowest level against the euro since November 1999 and slid versus most other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday on heightened worries about North Korea's nuclear ambitions. \par \par \uc2  The International Atomic Energy Agency confirmed that North Korea had asked its inspection staff to leave the country, the latest in a series of moves by the country toward possibly reviving its nuclear weapons program. \par \par \uc2  The United States urged North Korea to reverse its course, and said it would not negotiate in response to "threats or broken commitments." \par \par \uc2  Joe Francomano, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Erste Bank in New York, said North Korea's actions were "just another straw" working to break the back of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "In the context of all the crises that are going on, plus the weak U.S. stock market and the poor Christmas retail sales, the North Korea news is taking on a greater relevance," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen as the most vulnerable to global tensions, partly due to U.S. involvement in world hot spots such as Iraq and North Korea, but also because during times of uncertainty investors tend to favor countries cushioned by current account surpluses. The United States has a large current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  The euro smashed through several layers of resistance to reach levels against the dollar not seen since November 1999. By late afternoon in New York, it was trading up a half percent at $1.04034 , having earlier risen as high as $1.0443. \par \par \uc2  Against the safe haven Swiss franc, the dollar was off 0.77 percent at $1.3905 francs , a fresh four-year low. \par \par \uc2  WEAK STOCKS \par \par \uc2  Also weighing on the dollar was a fall in U.S. blue chips for the fourth straight day. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average  fell 1.5 percent, burdened by geopolitical worries, high oil prices, reports of weak retail sales at Christmas and soft corporate profits. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq Composite  eased 1.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  Light sweet crude oil traded in New York set two-week highs of $32.76 a barrel before settling modestly higher at $32.72 as Venezuela's general strike reached its 26th straight day. Gold prices also rose. \par \par \uc2  In a separate development, at least 46 people were killed when suspected Chechen rebel suicide bombers rammed vehicles packed with a ton of explosives into the local government headquarters in Grozny. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar, which has been on a firming trend versus the U.S. dollar since mid-November, also was succumbing to global political concerns. \par \par \uc2  "When geopolitical risks exist, the Canadian dollar trades like an emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There is no liquidity at year-end and that makes it even worse," said David Ebata, managing analyst at Thomson IFR in Boston. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was up 0.69 percent against its Canadian counterpart at C$1.5684 , its highest in a month. \par \par \uc2  Preoccupied as it is with global security concerns, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market paid little attention to U.S. housing sales data, which showed sales of new single-family homes as the highest on record in November. \par \par \uc2  Sales rose 5.7 percent to a 1,069,000 annual rate, more than the 1,000,000 rate expected by economists. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR HOLDS ITS OWN VERSUS YEN \par \par \uc2  Fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the dollar from falling against the yen kept the dollar well supported against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar barely moved against the Japanese yen, finishing the U.S. trading day at 119.85 yen , down just 0.7 percent from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is a little concerned about token \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  at below 120 yen," said Hugh Walsh, vice president at Fortis U.S.A. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials, worried that a strong yen would hurt its exports, have been talking down the yen for some time. \par \par \uc2  They stepped up their anti-yen rhetoric on Friday with Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa saying Japan must act if the yen started trending higher or if there were rapid movements in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  The country's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, also warned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements over the year-end and New Year period and that appropriate action would be taken if needed. \par \par \uc2  Countering these warnings were comments by Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, a well-known advocate of a strong yen, who argued against artificially weakening the yen to defeat the price deflation. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2133GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m. (22:30 GMT) in the\par previous New York session.\par Last  US Close    %      YTD     2001\par 26 Dec.  Change %Change    Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.0434   1.0378   +0.54  +17.18   0.8904\par Dlr/yen              119.85   119.93   -0.07   -8.95   131.63\par Euro/yen             125.07   124.43   +0.51   +6.68   117.24\par Dlr/swiss            1.3905   1.4013   -0.77  -16.20   1.6594\par Stg/dlr              1.6035   1.5996   +0.24  +10.27   1.4541\par Dlr/cad              1.5684   1.5576   +0.69   -1.46   1.5917\par Aus/dlr              0.5612   0.5632   -0.36   +9.91   0.5106\par Euro/swiss           1.4511   1.4541   -0.21   -1.82   1.4780\par Euro/stg             0.6504   0.6481   +0.35   +6.22   0.6123\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par Economic Forecasts...          Official rates...\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par European markets......\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021227dycr015ts\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
