\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar at new low vs euro as global tensions rise. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2002\par 18:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 27 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to its lowest level against the euro since November 1999 on Friday and eased against most other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on heightened worries about North Korea's nuclear ambitions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also crept lower versus the Swiss franc, in the process reaching a fresh four-year low, as investors sought a safe haven at a time of growing geopolitical uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  The International Atomic Energy Agency confirmed that North Korea had asked its inspection staff to leave the country. The IAEA said it was drafting a response. \par \par \uc2  The IAEA on Thursday said it had "serious nonproliferation concerns" after North Korea said it planned to restart a small nuclear reactor which had its use frozen in 1994 after a crisis over Pyongyang's nuclear arms ambitions. \par \par \uc2  "North Korea and Iraq are still the focus," said Hugh Walsh, vice president at Fortis U.S.A. in New York. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is weak across the board, and people continue to look at the Swiss franc especially as a safe haven," he said. \par \par \uc2  Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was off a half percent at $1.3941 francs . \par \par \uc2  It was down by about a third of a percent against the euro at $1.0411 per euro , having earlier gotten as low as $1.4019, its lowest level since hitting $1.0435 per euro on Nov. 18, 1999. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen as the most vulnerable to global tensions, partly due to U.S. involvement in world hot spots but also because during times of uncertainty, investors tend to favor countries cushioned by current account surpluses. The United States has a large current account deficit. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. stocks were trading lower at midday, burdened by geopolitical\par worries, persistently high oil prices and soft corporate profits. The\par Down Jones industrial average  was down 0.8 percent, while the Nasdaq\par Composite         had shed 0.7 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In a separate development, at least 40 people were killed in a blast on\par Friday at the local government headquarters in Grozny, capital of the\par rebellious Russian province of Chechnya.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The republic's acting prosecutor said it was not clear how many people\par had been injured when a truck and an off-road vehicle packed with a ton\par of explosives smashed into the building in central Grozny.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar, which has been on a firming trend versus the U.S.\par dollar since mid-November, also was succumbing to global political\par concerns.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "When geopolitical risks exist, the Canadian dollar trades like an\par emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . There is no liquidity at year-end and that\par makes it even worse," said David Ebata, managing analyst at Thomson IFR\par in Boston.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was up 0.66 percent against its Canadian counterpart at\par C$1.5679 , its highest in a month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. HOME SALES SHINE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Preoccupied as it is with global security concerns, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market paid little attention to U.S. home sales data, which\par showed sales of new single-family homes as the highest on record in\par November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sales rose 5.7 percent to a 1,069,000 annual rate, more than the\par 1,000,000 rate expected by economists. Sales were particularly robust\par in the Midwest, where they soared 41.2 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was similarly uninterested in news that Japanese industrial\par production fell a surprise 2.2 percent in November. Economists had\par predicted a far more modest 0.4 percent fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen seemingly has been immune to a raft of poor Japanese economic\par data recently as it too benefits from widespread bearishness toward the\par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the yen's gains have been stemmed by aggressive verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par from Japanese officials and fears that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could\par back up words with action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan is worried that a strong yen would hurt exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is a little concerned about token \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par at below 120 yen," said Walsh of Fortis U.S.A.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese monetary officials stepped up their anti-yen rhetoric on\par Friday with Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa saying Japan must act if\par the yen started trending higher or if there were rapid movements in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The country's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, also warned that\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would closely watch \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements over the\par year-end and New Year period and that appropriate action would be taken\par if needed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Countering these warnings were comments by Bank of Japan Governor\par Masaru Hayami, a well-known advocate of a strong yen, who argued\par against artificially weakening the yen to defeat the price deflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By late morning in New York, the dollar was flat versus the yen at\par 119.90 yen .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021227dycr00wki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
