\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits 4yr low vs Swissie,war nerves dominate. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2002\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The dollar extended losses in thin pre-holiday trade on Tuesday, setting a four-year low against the safe-haven Swiss franc as concerns of possible U.S.-led action against Iraq kept flows out of the greenback. \par \par \uc2  Oil prices shot up to their highest in two years earlier in Asian trade, with a continuing oil industry strike in Venezuela adding to concerns about disruption to supplies. \par \par \uc2  This further escalated investor risk aversion, with investors seeking capital protection unwinding their high-risk carry trades and putting funds into low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a large current account surplus. \par \par \uc2  "Risk reduction, concerns about a war and a lack of faith in the U.S. recovery are undermining not only the dollar but risk assets and risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well," said Paul Lambert, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Deutsche Asset Management. \par \par \uc2  "People are risk averse because of the prospect of a war. Before the war begins you never know what is going to happen. In these circumstances \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with large balance of payments surplus tend to do well." \par \par \uc2  By 1055 GMT the greenback had fallen to 1.4122 Swiss francs, its lowest since February 1999. Against the euro it fell to $1.0298, within less than half a cent of last week's three year trough. \par \par \uc2  The yen bounced to 120.09 per dollar, around half a yen off Monday's one-month peak. But it showed little reaction to news Japan had appointed Zembei Mizoguchi as its top financial diplomat at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  from next year, succeeding Haruhiko Kuroda. \par \par \uc2  POSITIONING FOR WAR \par \par \uc2  Following the move higher in the franc, the Swiss National Bank said it was worried about a rapid euro decline but added that the drop in the dollar was related to thin end-of-year markets. \par \par \uc2  The SNB has already warned the bank has room to cut rates if the franc surges further, threatening economic growth. \par \par \uc2  However, in an environment of high investor risk aversion, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a large current account surplus tend to perform well as investors bring their funds back home. \par \par \uc2  The yen is another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which benefits in such an environment. Data out earlier showed Japan's custom-cleared trade surplus rose for the ninth straight month in November, gaining a bigger than expected 80.9 percent from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  In the United States, Defense Secretary Donald Rumsfeld said on Monday that U.S. forces were capable of handling conflict with North Korea and Iraq at the same time. \par \par \uc2  He cautioned North Korea against using the current world focus on Iraq to indulge nuclear brinkmanship but also said diplomacy still seemed the best way to deal with the communist state. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar remains on the backfoot with a continued slew of comments coming out from the U.S. administration," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  Markets are also keeping an eye on any developments on the Iraq front given news on Monday Iraqi forces had shot down an unmanned U.S. spy plane. \par \par \uc2  On the economic front, U.S. durable goods figures are due at 1330 GMT and forecast to have risen 0.7 percent in November after rising 2.4 in October. \par \par \uc2  European markets will wind down early on Tuesday and the U.S. bond market association has recommended early closing. London has a two-day break before business resumes on Friday. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN APPOINTMENT \par \par \uc2  In Japan, Mizoguchi is expected to take over from Kuroda before a new parliamentary session begins late next month. He will be replaced at the Finance Ministry's International Bureau by his deputy, Hiroshi Watanabe. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda has kept a low profile in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in recent months and Tokyo traders expect his successor will as well. \par \par \uc2  "It was much expected. The tone of their comments may differ slightly but we will have to wait and see until he actually takes up his post," said Takashi Toyahara, a manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  Wariness \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem any export-damaging yen rise against the dollar was helping to underpin the greenback at 120 and below. Analysts noted Japanese monetary authorities were not averse to taking action in holiday-thinned markets. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021224dyco00lgg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
