\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hovers near lows, conflict caution subdues. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Charlotte Cooper \par \uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2002\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The dollar held close to recent multi-year lows against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday as Europe wound down for holidays in a mood made cautious by increasing concerns of possible U.S.-led action against Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The market took in its stride comments from U.S. Defense Secretary Donald Rumsfeld on Monday that U.S. forces were capable of handling conflict with North Korea and Iraq at the same time. \par \par \uc2  The dollar held in tight ranges close to a recent four-year low against the safe-haven Swiss franc, a three-year trough on the euro and a one-month low on the yen. \par \par \uc2  News Japan had appointed Zembei Mizoguchi as its top financial diplomat at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  from next year, succeeding Haruhiko Kuroda, failed to galvanise Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar remains on the backfoot with a continued slew of comments coming out from the U.S. administration," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategiest at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is doing well and the Swissie is underpinned by safe haven flows." \par \par \uc2  By 0900 GMT the dollar was at $1.0270 per euro less than a cent above last week's three year trough. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc was at 1.4165 per dollar, close to Monday's near-four year high, while the yen stood at 120.35 per dollar, around half a yen off Monday's one-month peak. \par \par \uc2  Underlining market jitters over the potential for Iraq-U.S. conflict in the new year, oil prices hit their highest in two years, with a freeze in deliveries from strike-bound Venezuela adding to concerns of disruptions to supplies. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN APPOINTMENT \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi is expected to take over from Kuroda before a new parliamentary session begins late next month. He will be replaced at the Finance Ministry's International Bureau by his deputy, Hiroshi Watanabe. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda has kept a low profile in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in recent months and Tokyo traders expect his successor will as well. \par \par \uc2  "I don't expect a big policy shift at all," said Toshihiko Masaki, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at China Construction Bank's Tokyo branch. \par \par \uc2  Takashi Toyahara, a manager at Nomura Securities, said: "It was much expected. The tone of their comments may differ slightly but we will have to wait and see until he actually takes up his post." \par \par \uc2  Wariness \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem any export-damaging yen rise against the dollar was helping to subdue trade and underpin the greenback at 120 and below. Analysts noted Japanese monetary authorities were not averse to taking action in holiday-thinned markets. \par \par \uc2  U.S. FOCUS \par \par \uc2  Rumsfeld cautioned North Korea against using the current world focus on Iraq to indulge nuclear brinkmanship but also said diplomacy still seemed the best way to deal with the communist state. \par \par \uc2  With no new developments on the Iraq front, after news on Monday Iraqi forces had shot down an unmanned U.S. spy plane, the main U.S. focus was data due at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  U.S. durable goods figures are forecast to have risen 0.7 percent in November after rising 2.4 in October. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Lucas Papademos told an Athens newspaper the main challenge of ECB monetary policy was to achieve and maintain price stability in 2003 and beyond and contribute to supporting a faster rate of economic growth. \par \par \uc2  Papademos said there were favourable prospects for a fall in eurozone inflation below two percent provided fuel prices did not rise further and wage increases continued to be contained. \par \par \uc2  EU Economic Affairs Commissioner Pedro Solbes said in an interview published on Tuesday that he favoured a strong euro, which would help to keep inflation low and give the ECB more scope to act on monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  European markets will wind down early on Tuesday and the U.S. bond market association has recommended early closing. \par \par \uc2  London has a two-day break before business resumes on Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021224dyco00hr1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
