\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr's Weakness Puts  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Back On The Cards \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry \par \uc2 1,117 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2002\par 21:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar's latest stumble has once again dramatically raised the odds of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, in a bid to haul the yen back on to a weakening track, U.S.-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said Monday. \par \par \uc2  Following some stern rhetoric from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier Monday, traders warn that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - in which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts on the finance ministry's behalf - are a strong possibility, even with the dollar having bounced back somewhat against the yen  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "They might want to time their next \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a period of maximum impact," when trading volumes are low, said Anne Parker Mills, senior U.S. economist with Brown Brothers Harriman in New York. Already, "there are pretty good odds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen does not retreat pretty  quickly and a high probability" if the dollar slumps below Y120.00, Mills said. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts believe the BOJ might also seek to act to act soon in order to take advantage of the relative limbo in  the U.S. Treasury, before the Senate confirmation of John Snow to replace Paul O'Neill as Treasury Secretary. Although  there's little to suggest that Snow will publicly embrace a  weaker dollar, many analysts believe he will continue to keep the so-called strong dollar policy vague, which could potentially work against any Japanese efforts to bolster the  \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, if Snow make a relatively strong statement supporting a more robust dollar, that would render  any prior BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  much more successful, heightening the advantage for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in moving ahead of Snow's confirmation, which will likely take place in January. \par \par \uc2  Although the dollar has stabilized somewhat against the yen Monday in New York at Y121.37, up from Y120.54 late Friday, it hasn't recovered much from its steep losses over the past few sessions, grabbing the attention of senior Japanese officials. The dollar has lost about 3.6% against the yen over the past ten days; on Friday alone, the dollar declined by over two yen. \par \par \uc2  "A rise of five yen in a week is a rapid move," Toshiro Mutoh, Administrative Vice Minister at the MOF, said  Monday, adding the MOF was prepared to take "firm action" against market volatility. Senior vice finance minister Takayoshi Taniguchi also warned that if the yen rose further, the authorities would take "decisive action." \par \par \uc2  This latest chorus appears particularly threatening to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants in the context of Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa's staggering remark earlier this month that Y150.00 or Y160.00 would be an appropriate level for the dollar; worlds away from its current range. The last time the dollar was even close to that level against the yen was when it reached a peak of around Y147.00 in August 1998. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Shiokawa Effect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese premier Junichiro Koizumi later only firmed a sense that\par Japan was actively seeking to promote a weak yen as its key economic\par tool, amid a relatively slow approach to  other structural reform, such\par as addressing the deep problems in the banking system. Indeed, another\par reason why strategists believe that MOF officials may be more trigger\par happy than when the ministry last staged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the end of\par June lies in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's deteriorating economic outlook, which makes the\par government even more anxious to shore up exporters' fortunes - a point\par not lost on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With trade thinning ahead of the year-end holidays, the chances of the\par BOJ stepping into the market "are definitely  increasing...they have\par given the verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  threat," said Tim Mazanec, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with Investors Bank & Trust in Boston.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the dollar should slip below the Y120.00 mark, following its sharp\par move lower on Friday, that further raises the chances of actual\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while in scant markets, "you get more bang for your buck,"\par so the effects  of any such action could be quite marked on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par Mazanec added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Japanese finance ministry considers speed of moves to be as\par important as absolute levels when deciding on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Even so,\par there is little doubt that a steeper  slip of the dollar to a key\par technical support area at Y119.10 would hit "a very critical lower\par boundary" that likely could precipitate BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Jan\par Poser, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign  exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research with Bank Sarasin in Zurich,\par Switzerland.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    One Eye On The Euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It's equally important to watch out for euro slippage against the\par Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Poser said. A retreat of the euro below the Y123.00\par mark could finally nudge Japanese government officials to shift from\par heightened rhetoric to action, Poser says. The euro was at Y124.07\par Monday afternoon  in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Short-term, the possibility of the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par buying dollars for yen, with its unlimited amount of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par will give traders sweaty palms.  Yet despite the BOJ's daunting capacity\par to whiplash markets  over the next few weeks when trading desks are\par lightly staffed, the perennial question remains whether such action\par would have any lasting effect. "Over the years, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par haven't done that much good," said Parker Mills.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in May and June, to the total tune of about\par $30 billion were, at best, a partial success, as they have succeeded in\par delaying the yen's rebound back to  the area that prompted such action\par earlier this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Then, as now, the Japanese government found itself swimming against a\par tide of negative dollar sentiment. Yet some new ingredients contributing\par to the dollar's demise may  conspire to make that tide even harder to\par turn now, strategists warn. The looming possibility of a war with Iraq\par could bruise the dollar against the Swiss franc, and inflame bouts of\par broader dollar weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par What's more, the BOJ has a bit of checkered history in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  realm. In September 2001, concerned that a strong yen might\par snuff out a nascent recovery in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly,\par buying dollars, as well as euro, for yen. Although, the bank lost the\par element of surprise by its regular appearances in the market, it did\par manage to ultimately push the dollar higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the period between January 1999 and April 2000 however, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into the market at least 18 times. But the market largely\par ignored the waves of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the yen continued to strengthen,\par hitting almost Y100 to the dollar by April 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By John Parry; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020021216dycg007vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
