\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Shiokawa backs hands-off approach to yen, yuan. \b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2002\par 09:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 5 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates were a crucial factor for price levels but that governments should not manipulate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa also said the fate of the Chinese yuan should be left to China itself, in response to calls for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be revalued to prevent the country from exporting deflation. \par \par \uc2  With Japan mired in deflation for four years, even though the Bank of Japan has kept interest rates at virtually zero, many experts have urged the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen to help boost domestic prices. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, it tumbled across the board with investors persuaded that the government is serious about pushing it down. \par \par \uc2  But Shiokawa said he stood by the policy of letting the market decide \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates - even though \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the exchange market more often than any other developed countries in recent years. \par \par \uc2  "There is no question that price levels must be increased. We do think \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are one factor, but we think governments should refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  or using policy measures to affect them," Shiokawa told parliament. \par \par \uc2  "Our basic policy is that they (rates) should be determined in markets." \par \par \uc2  CHINA POLICY \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa stressed that other countries should not interfere with Chinese policy and any decision on the yuan - which is virtually pegged to the U.S. dollar - was up to China, whose domestic prices are falling and exports rapidly growing. \par \par \uc2  "China itself is suffering from deflation," he said. "The desirable thing is for the nation and the government authorities to acknowledge that revaluing the yuan is in its interest." \par \par \uc2  Dai Xianglong, governor of the central People's Bank of China, told a financial conference on Wednesday that China would continue to keep the yuan stable. His remarks followed comments by Finance Minister Xiang Huaicheng last month that the yuan was under upward pressure. \par \par \uc2  A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally puts a downward pressure on a nation's domestic prices, but Shiokawa did not elaborate on why a floatation would be in Beijing's interest. \par \par \uc2  "It is true that there are imbalances among \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of all the countries. I'm not talking just about China's problem, but one factor in China's problem is the imbalance and I have mentioned this at Group of Seven discussions," he added. \par \par \uc2  "There is another meeting soon - next month - so I would like to bring this up again." \par \par \uc2  He said he wanted China to look at purchasing power parity (PPP), a comparison of prices of similar goods in different countries. \par \par \uc2  Last weekend, Shiokawa said in a speech that the yen should be at around 150-160 to the dollar from a PPP point of view, sparking a drop in the yen to beyond 125 to the dollar this week from around 122.50 at the end of last week. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this week, the Finance Ministry's top diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda wrote in an opinion piece on the Financial Times that China was exporting deflation, with its export growth and a combination of a price deflation and a fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021205dyc500gu4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
