\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen dives as Japan FinMin triggers bear rampage. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2002\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The yen dived to a three-year low against the euro and a five-week low against the dollar on Monday as comments from Japan's finance minister that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overvalued spurred yen bears into action. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa was quoted in a Japanese newspaper as saying that the yen was excessively strong and that it should be around 150-160 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Selling snowballed in thin European trade, knocking Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than two yen down to 124.80 per dollar - on track for its sharpest one-day fall since July. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders love targets and Shiokawa has given them just that," said Neal Kimberley, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "People now see the yen as a one-way bet and are jumping on the bandwagon." \par \par \uc2  Added fuel to the fire, Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda used a commentary in Monday's Financial Times to urge the Bank of Japan to set an inflation target and called for coordinated reflation policies. \par \par \uc2  "It's clearer now than before that Japan wants a weaker yen," said Stephen Jen, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Morgan Stanley. \par \par \uc2  The yen also fell more than one percent to a three-year low of 123.48 against the euro, but the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to keep pace with the dollar's gains and hit a one-month low around $0.9860. \par \par \uc2  PLAYING WITH FIRE \par \par \uc2  Identifying a target for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates is dangerous for any finance minister, but \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tradition of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  meant Shiokawa's comments were taken particularly seriously by the market. \par \par \uc2  Japan has called for a weaker yen on several occasions in recent months and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this this year and September last year. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa's comments have spurred the market to take new positions against the yen," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  "Not only is he clearly saying he wants to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker, he is stipulating ranges." \par \par \uc2  Many analysts say a weak-yen policy, which would aid exporters, is one of the few options left to Japan to dig itself out of its economic slump. Interest rates are already near zero and the government's huge debts restrict its ability to spend its way out of trouble. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese finance ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi suggested Shiokawa may have been referring to purchasing power parity estimates, but his comments did little to soften the blow. \par \par \uc2  "There's little doubt that Japan needs a weaker yen and if Shiokawa put a number on it, he did so deliberately," said Kimberley. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR BUOYANT \par \par \uc2  The dollar maintained its firmer tone, with U.S. data later in the day expected to reinforce the view that the world's biggest economy is on the path to recovery. \par \par \uc2  The prospect of a strong Wall Street open also buoyed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with U.S. stock futures up around 1.5 percent in European trade. \par \par \uc2  The Institute for Supply Management's U.S. manufacturing index is due at 1500 GMT and is expected to rise to 51.3 in November from 48.5 in October. \par \par \uc2  In contrast the Reuters Eurozone Purchasing Managers' Index held below the critical 50 line that divides expansion from contraction and retail sales in the euro zone posted their biggest monthly drop in September since March 2000. \par \par \uc2  The market widely expects the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates by up to 50 basis points when it meets on Thursday in an attempt to reinvigorate the economy. \par \par \uc2  ECB officials have been sending strong signals they are ready to ease for the first time in over a year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021202dyc200ph1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
