\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar powers to one-month high against yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2002\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The dollar powered to a one-month high on the yen on Monday, fuelled by a brighter outlook for the U.S economy and signs that Japan was talking down its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  Reported comments from Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa pepped up the dollar in early Asian trade. He was quoted in a local newspaper as saying that the yen was excessively strong and that it should be around 150-160 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Most traders dismissed the range as too far off current levels to be a realistic target but a bout of speculative bids helped trip some stop-loss buying, pushing the dollar to as high as 123.42 yen its best since October 29. \par \par \uc2  By midday, the dollar hovered at 123.32/34 yen compared with 122.44 in late New York trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yen was also down against the euro, with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up at 122.37/43 yen from 121.85 in New York. Against the dollar, the euro hovered at 99.22/24 cents from 99.49. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa's comments were only taken half-seriously in the markets, but we saw some speculative buying, which could also be explained by expectations of better U.S. growth," said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Adding to the dollar's buoyancy were hopes that the week's set of U.S. economic data would cement the view that the U.S. economy was on a steady path for recovery. \par \par \uc2  Monday sees the Institute for Supply Management's U.S. manufacturing index, expected to rise to 51.3 in November against 48.5 in October. Jobs data for November are due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Another focus is how enthusiastic U.S. consumers will be about their holiday shopping and some surveys showed that sales got off to a good start over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  KURODA, ECB \par \par \uc2  Analysts said any impact from Shiokawa's reported comments would prove short-lived unless the Japanese authorities stepped in with actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japanese officials have tended to favour a weaker yen to bolster exports. \par \par \uc2  "Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ineffective," said Toru Umemoto, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "What we need for a weaker yen is policy coordination, meaning the disposal of banks' bad debt, an inflation target from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) and unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on track for such action, but it's not quite there yet," Umemoto said. \par \par \uc2  A commentary from Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, in the Financial Times, also aroused interest with its call for coordinated reflation policies from the United States, Europe and Japan to avoid a deflationary spiral. \par \par \uc2  But he said concerted action should only have a limited impact on exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  Calling on the BOJ to adopt an inflation target, Kuroda also wrote that monetary easing in Europe was desirable. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) is expected to cut interest rates when its board meets on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  ECB council memeber Ernst Welteke said on Friday that euro zone price stability was not in danger. \par \par \uc2  "A 25 basis point rate cut is a done deal," said Umemoto at Morgan Stanley, adding that if the ECB were to cut by 50 basis points, it would prove supportive for the euro. No action would be a sell-factor for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...        Debt...      Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021202dyc2008hr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
