\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slips from highs, cushioned by bank worries. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2002\par 08:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 19 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped from earlier highs against the yen in Asia on Tuesday as uncertainty over Iraq weighed, but selling was limited due to growing concerns over Japanese banks. \par \par \uc2  The greenback briefly rose to a session high of 121.20 yen after confusing comments from Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa spurred speculation of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said that he wanted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to leave its yen fund supply to the banking system "unsterilised". \par \par \uc2  Some players took that to mean he was urging the BOJ to further ease its monetary policy - seen as a yen-selling factor - and covered dollar-short positions, pushing down the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa's comments initially gave an impression that he was aggressive about \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which triggered short-covering, but if you take a look at his comments closely he didn't mean that," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa later clarified his comments, saying that he wanted the BOJ to refrain from absorbing excess yen funds created by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the government decided to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Asked by Reuters whether the ministry was considering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Shiokawa said: "We are not." \par \par \uc2  Asked if he wanted the BOJ to leave \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds unsterilised, he said: "Yes." \par \par \uc2  At 0701 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 120.98/1.01 yen against 120.93 in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  LITTLE REACTION TO BOJ \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction after the BOJ's nine-member Policy Board decided to tweak the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key monetary target, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The board said it would keep the target for financial institutions' current account deposits parked at the BOJ in a 15-20 trillion yen ($125-166 billion) range but would aim to keep the amount at the upper end of the target rather than the middle. \par \par \uc2  "In an oral agreement, they decided to aim for 20 trillion yen, the upper end of the 15-20 trillion yen range, and try to achieve as high a level as possible," a BOJ official said. \par \par \uc2  Economists said that by targeting the upper end, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to soothe rising concerns about banking sector instability in the wake of new government reforms to tackle the nation's chronic bad loan problem. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the BOJ's move was unlikely to help the ailing economy. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's TOPIX index closed at an 18-year low on Tuesday as investors dumped banking stocks on growing fears that the weaker banks may be nationalised as part of the government's plan to clean up their massive bad loans. \par \par \uc2  UFJ Holdings Inc , Japan's smallest megabank, tumbled 10.1 percent, or by its daily limit of 10,000 yen, to a record low of 89,000 yen. \par \par \uc2  Mizuho Holdings Inc , the world's biggest bank by assets, plunged 16.22 percent to an all-time closing low of 99,700 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Renewed concerns over financial systems in Japan have been a factor in lifting the dollar from the low of 119.10 yen last week, but the market simply lacks incentives to drive it up further now," Nomura's Toyahara said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at $1.0091/97 compared with $1.0090 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 121.96/2.06 yen against 122.13 yen. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, some dollar bears think the greenback could come under pressure from U.S. trade data to be released at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists in a Reuters survey forecast, on average, a $37.33 billion deficit in September compared with a $38.46 billion deficit in August, but some traders said a higher deficit could prompt dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the greenback stood at 1.4549/54 Swiss francs against late U.S. level of 1.4538/48. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was little changed at $1.5811/17 against $1.5813/23. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021119dybj00ack\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
