\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - CORRECTED-WRAPUP 1-Japan c/a surplus falls, export slowdown a co. \b0\par\par\uc2 882 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2002\par 03:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In TOKYO story headlined "WRAPUP 1-Japan c/a surplus falls,\par  export slowdown a concern" please read in 26th paragraph ....a\par  reaction to a hefty fall in August.... instead of ....a reaction\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a strong gain in August (making clear that machinery orders fell in\par August).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  A corrected story follows. \par \par \uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The surplus on Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, fell for the first time in a year in September as slowing exports threatened to remove the main prop from an economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Monday showed that the current account surplus fell 6.8 percent in September from a year earlier to 1.1705 trillion yen ($9.76 billion), putting an end to 11 straight months of growth and falling short of market forecasts. \par \par \uc2  Economists had expected a surplus of about 1.28 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  Gross domestic product figures for July-September, to be released on Wednesday, are likely to show slight growth for the quarter, but some economists expect that to be the last growth for some time as Japan feels the chill from a global slowdown and particularly from a stuttering U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  Most economists expect net exports to make a negative contribution to GDP for the first time in a year. \par \par \uc2  The trade surplus grew 2.0 percent from a year earlier to 1.1955 trillion yen, the pace of growth slowing from earlier this year in line with weaker exports. \par \par \uc2  "It was clear from the customs-cleared trade figures a couple of weeks ago that the surplus has petered out in September, particularly in trade in goods," said Shuji Shirota, an economist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. \par \par \uc2  Those figures showed exports down by 2.3 percent in September from the previous month in seasonally adjusted terms. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the current account surplus fell for the first time in a year shows that the prospect of an export-led economic recovery is receding," Shirota said. \par \par \uc2  "In fact, GDP figures on Wednesday will likely show that net exports in July-September were down from the previous quarter." \par \par \uc2  Rapid export growth that fuelled Japan's recovery from recession earlier this year is showing signs of stalling on the back of stagnant consumer demand in the United States, Japan's biggest export market. \par \par \uc2  For the six months to September, the current account rose 25.4 percent from a year earlier, the Finance Ministry said. \par \par \uc2  Recently, though, major high-tech exporters such as Hitachi Ltd and Fujitsu Ltd have been cutting earnings targets, and economists say a slackening in exports could tip Japan back into recession later this year. \par \par \uc2  YEN RISE SPARKS CONCERN \par \par \uc2  Exports in the coming months are likely to be further hit by the U.S. west coast port lock-out that severly disrupted trade with the United States in September and October. \par \par \uc2  The trade figures came as the yen climbed near two-month highs against to around 119.54 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Growing tension between the United States and Iraq helped send the dollar lower late last week, putting traders on alert for possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Finance Ministry. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, said on Monday morning that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements had been "totally inappropriate". \par \par \uc2  Separate data released by the Bank of Japan showed little change in monetary conditions as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to pump massive amounts of liquidity into the banking system fail to filter through to the real economy. \par \par \uc2  The most widely watched measures of money supply, M2 plus certificates of deposit, rose 3.3 percent in October from a year earlier, maintaining its steady rise. \par \par \uc2  Lending by the three main categories of Japanese banks fell 5.2 percent in October from a year earlier, the 58th straight month of decline. \par \par \uc2  Paralysed by trillions of yen in bad loans, banks have been reluctant to embark on new lending and have tended to keep the extra liquidity from the BOJ for themselves. \par \par \uc2  The government has attempted to tackle the problem with a recent report on bank reform, but many analysts are sceptical whether its harsher aspects will be implemented. \par \par \uc2  The government also said that the domestic wholesale price index was down 0.1 percent in October from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  Deflation has been eating away at consumer confidence and company profits for at lest three years, and shows few signs of abating. \par \par \uc2  Economists are expecting the slowdown in exports to have a knock-on effect on industrial production, and machinery orders data for September due out later in the day will be closely watched for signs of this. \par \par \uc2  Core orders, an indicator of capital spending, are expected to have risen 5.2 percent in September after sliding a month earlier, a Reuters poll of 20 economists showed on Friday, but that would mostly be a reaction to a hefty fall in August. \par \par \uc2  For the whole third quarter, the government estimates machinery orders fell 3.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll of 25 economists showed the economy probably expanded by a slight 0.4 percent in July-September as a modest rise in consumer spending offset a fall in exports. \par \par \uc2  ($1=119.90 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021111dybb00412\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
