\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  set to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if dollar keeps slipping. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2002\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 8 (Reuters) - Japanese monetary authorities are expected to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to try to lift the dollar so as to help protect Japanese exports should it continue its slide towards 120 yen, dealers and analysts say. \par \par \uc2  The dollar inched down on Friday to a level not seen in two months, fuelling talk about if and when Japanese monetary authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's outlook was increasingly bearish due to the U.S. Federal Reserve's surprising half-point rate cut on Wednesday, tensions surrounding Iraq and a volatile U.S. equity market. \par \par \uc2  All of those factors are expected to push the dollar down towards 120 yen and many dealers noted that officials at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) were growing tense about the yen's current level. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities worry that a stronger yen could choke off growth in exports and derail an export-led economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "Although the market consensus now is that the yen has not come to a critical level yet that would prompt the authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many consider 120 yen a critical level," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president at \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group at UFJ Bank. \par \par \uc2  There was also a speculation that the authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  even at the current level of around 121 yen. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's latest "tankan" quarterly survey of corporate sentiment, issued in early October, showed big manufacturers used an average rate of 120.82 yen to the dollar for the October-March second half of the business year for sales and profit forecasts. \par \par \uc2  MORE TENSE \par \par \uc2  But Sahara said many exporters have already fulfilled their dollar-selling needs towards the new year, so pressure from the dollar's recent fall is limited for the time being. \par \par \uc2  The dollar edged down to 120.81 yen on Friday morning in Asia, its lowest level since mid-September. By mid-afternoon it hovered above 121 yen. \par \par \uc2  The authorities last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 28, when the dollar slipped below 119 yen. \par \par \uc2  The MOF said Japan spent a total of 4.0162 trillion yen ($33.14 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during April-June, the largest amount for any quarter since it started disclosing such data in 1991. \par \par \uc2  Authorities have kept out of the market since then, even when the dollar fell to 115.50 yen in mid-July. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said authorities may be more tense now as Japan could face further deflationary pressure amid efforts to clean up non-performing loans in the financial sector, officially estimated at 52 trillion yen ($427.5 billion). \par \par \uc2  A member of the Bank of Japan's Policy board, Teizo Taya, said on Thursday he could accept a weaker yen if deflationary pressures increased, as a rising yen would likely exacerbate SUCH pressures. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, for his part, told parliament on Thursday that the government should not interfere with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and exchange rates should be determined by markets. \par \par \uc2  Whatever the intention, most see the dollar continuing to fall regardless of whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buys dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the dollar is falling on its own bearish factors, talking down the yen or actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't work," said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108dyb800aci\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\tr